{{author's notes:

and here we have it, the third entry in the "Liar's Heraldry Triptych"

i actually believe i like this piece the least, haha. not because the underlying gem of potential is bad, but ... because i *was* actually playing the victim when i wrote this

the point of this story was to showcase that i wasn't the kind of person who would run away from difficult emotional challenges *in spite of* the fact that the narrator clearly believed themselves to be the kind of person who would and did run away

an interesting challenge that I completely failed at

again, i was dishonest, this time about my own hand in the wreckage around me. i complained about all the betrayals of trust i'd endured, but never once admitted to my own hand in harm suffered by others. i was playing the victim

i literally ran away from the difficult emotional challenge of being honest

yes, i know, i should be kind

but these stories are bad because i was weak, and i can admit that}}

